1
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:09,518
In episode one I said: a candle hides three things.

2
00:00:09,969 --> 00:00:15,219
Where most trading happened, who was aggressive, and who got trapped.

3
00:00:15,670 --> 00:00:20,424
Today, the chart that shows the candle from the inside: the footprint.

4
00:00:21,424 --> 00:00:26,335
Hello, this is episode twelve of the SPIDER Order Flow series.

5
00:00:26,784 --> 00:00:32,662
Last time: Time and Sales, the tape. One line per trade.

6
00:00:33,113 --> 00:00:38,102
Today: the footprint. The same data, arranged inside the candle.

7
00:00:39,102 --> 00:00:43,543
A footprint is a candle opened up to show its inside.

8
00:00:43,993 --> 00:00:48,199
At each price of the candle it shows how much volume traded there.

9
00:00:48,649 --> 00:00:53,899
So thousands of tape lines, added up by price, in one place.

10
00:00:54,899 --> 00:00:58,870
Each price has two numbers with a cross between them.

11
00:00:59,320 --> 00:01:05,275
The left number: volume traded at the bid. Sellers sold with market orders.

12
00:01:05,726 --> 00:01:11,603
The right number: volume traded at the ask. Buyers bought with market orders.

13
00:01:12,053 --> 00:01:17,121
An easy way to remember: left is the sellers, right is the buyers.

14
00:01:18,121 --> 00:01:24,234
Let us read one row. At 102 it says: 120 x 260.

15
00:01:24,684 --> 00:01:32,651
It means at this price aggressive sellers sold 120 lots and aggressive buyers bought 260 lots.

16
00:01:33,101 --> 00:01:35,217
Buyers were heavier here.

17
00:01:36,217 --> 00:01:38,985
A footprint is shown in three ways.

18
00:01:39,436 --> 00:01:43,955
First, bid-ask: both numbers, as we just saw.

19
00:01:44,405 --> 00:01:52,110
Second, delta: ask minus bid at each price. At 102, +140.

20
00:01:52,561 --> 00:01:59,327
Third, volume: total volume at each price. At 102, 380.

21
00:02:00,327 --> 00:02:05,969
Now we read the whole candle. Step one: find the row with the most volume.

22
00:02:06,419 --> 00:02:11,487
Here that is 102. It is called the POC of the candle.

23
00:02:11,937 --> 00:02:17,579
So the real business of this candle happened here, not at the top or bottom ends.

24
00:02:18,579 --> 00:02:21,819
Step two: the delta of the whole candle.

25
00:02:22,269 --> 00:02:29,583
All the right numbers add up to 655. All the left numbers add up to 390.

26
00:02:30,033 --> 00:02:35,519
Delta is +265. Aggressive buyers led in this candle.

27
00:02:36,519 --> 00:02:39,523
Step three: look at the ends of the candle.

28
00:02:39,972 --> 00:02:46,660
At the very top, at 104: 80 x 30. Sellers are heavier here.

29
00:02:47,109 --> 00:02:54,268
So at the top of a green candle, buyers weakened. That is what a plain candle hides.

30
00:02:55,268 --> 00:03:02,504
So the reading order: where the POC is, which side the delta is on, and who is heavier at the ends.

31
00:03:02,954 --> 00:03:09,719
If the POC is in the upper part, business happened at higher prices. If lower, then lower.

32
00:03:10,168 --> 00:03:15,498
Do not decide from one candle. Read it with nearby candles and the level.

33
00:03:16,498 --> 00:03:22,298
And the same truth again: spot forex and gold have no real footprint.

34
00:03:22,748 --> 00:03:29,017
A footprint needs the real volume and side of every trade, which only an exchange provides.

35
00:03:29,466 --> 00:03:35,998
So read footprints on futures: gold futures, index futures, or a crypto exchange.

36
00:03:36,998 --> 00:03:38,565
So, today's summary.

37
00:03:39,015 --> 00:03:46,826
A footprint shows the candle from inside. Each price has bid x ask: left sellers, right buyers.

38
00:03:47,275 --> 00:03:51,481
Three types: bid-ask, delta and volume.

39
00:03:51,930 --> 00:04:00,369
Three reading steps: POC, candle delta, and the ends. Real footprints come from futures.

40
00:04:01,369 --> 00:04:06,698
